        "original_id": "29c0c754-8ac2-5def-984b-2e42c9d72908",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Æthelweard, Æthelred I of Wessex, Alfred the Great, Cynric\n- Roles: ealdorman, historian, king\n- Works: Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, Chronicon Æthelweardi\n- Topics: Anglo-Saxon history, annals, Old English, Latin\n\nFacts:\n- The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle is a collection of annals in Old English that chronicles the history of the Anglo-Saxons.\n- Everything known about Cynric comes from the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle.\n- Æthelweard, who died around 998, was descended from Æthelred I of Wessex, the elder brother of Alfred the Great.\n- Æthelweard was an ealdorman and the author of a Latin version of the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle known as the Chronicon Æthelweardi.",
